      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "Boom colt LOUCASSO (8) made it three from three at this circuit and distance since joining Seaton Grima for this campaign when he took out a heat of this series by 2.3m last start. Draws wider but had enough speed to lead and win well from similar barriers in his other two outings since a long spell. Has been kept up to the mark with an easy trial win and is the one to beat. NOCTURNAL (5) was held up when runner-up here last week and had made it three wins on the trot with his fresh success at Newcastle prior. Runs into a smart one tonight but he is capable and should be close to his peak now. LEXY (1) came from the back row to beat a handy one when resuming at Bathurst. The ace draw can see him competitive. UPTOWN CHANCE (10) cops a wide draw but is worth including after winning two of his last three outings, one of them at this circuit and distance.",
